      "message": "You got me 😊\n\nHow about:\n```\n+/*\n+ * Convert number to string.\n+ *\n+ * NOTE: tmp[20] is sized specifically for 64-bit numbers in base 10 (max 20 digits)\n+ * and base 16 (max 16 digits). Other bases are not supported.\n+ */\n static char *number(char *str, char *end, unsigned long long num, int base,\n {\n        static const char digits[16] \u003d \"0123456789abcdef\";\n        char tmp[20];\n        int i \u003d 0;\n \n+       /* Currently only base 10 and 16 are supported */\n+       if (base !\u003d 10 \u0026\u0026 base !\u003d 16)\n+               return str;\n```\n?",
